. dan Slamin (2000), Edge-magic total la-\nbelings, Australas. J. Combin., 22, 177 - 190.\nWallis, W. D., (2001), Magic Graphs, Birkhuser.\nWijaya, K. dan Baskoro, E. T. (2000), Edge-magic total labeling on disconnected\ngraphs, Proc. of the eleventh australasian workshop on combinatorial algo-\nrithms, 139 - 144.\n101--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSuper Edge - Magic Strength of Fire Crackers, Banana Trees and Unicyclic Graphs | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220187652_Super_Edge_-_Magic_Strength_of_Fire_Crackers_Banana_Trees_and_Unicyclic_Graphs)\nciteturn5search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 20.4 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; In 2006, Swaminathan and Jeyanthi [11] determined the sm(G) where G can be unicyclic graphs, fire crackers and banana trees.\n\n# Super Edge - Magic Strength of Fire Crackers, Banana Trees and Unicyclic Graphs\n\n  * July 2006\n  * Electronic Notes in Discrete Mathematics 306(14):1624-1636\n\nDOI:10.1016/S1571-0653(04)00582-7\n\n  * Source\n  * DBLP\n\nAuthors:\n\nV. Swaminathan\n\nV. Swaminathan\n\n  * This person is not on ResearchGate, or hasn't claimed this research yet.\n\nJeyanthi P.\n\n  * Govindammal Aditanar College for Women,Tiruchendur,Tamilnadu,INDIA\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nA graph G (V, E) is called super edge-magic if there exists a bijection f from V ∪ E to { 1, 2, 3, ..., | V | + | E | } such that f (u) + f (v) + f (uv) = c (f) is constant for any uv ∈ E and f (V) = { 1, 2, 3, ..., | V | }. Such a bijection is called a super edge-magic labeling of G. The super edge-magic strength of a graph G is defined as the minimum of all c (f) where the minimum runs over all super edge-magic labelings of G and is denoted by sm (G). The super edge-magic strength of some families of graphs are obtained in this paper.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2116] M. Sundaram, R. Ponraj, and S. Somasundram, Total product cordia